  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-001 — first cut of @m0saic/alpine/leaderboard/v1 (the 6th Alpine template). A ranked list in the white card: each row is a small rounded RANK BADGE (gold/silver/bronze for the podium, muted grey below) + name + value. Rows AUTO-SORT by value descending so the rank reflects the score (preSorted keeps your order); the top 3 get a soft medal-tinted row wash (podiumTint). Values count up; valueLabel overrides the auto number (with valuePrefix/suffix for '$' / ' pts'). Built on the bar-graph/progress model — splits + rounded tiles, no inline-masks — and every height weight is snapped to a multiple of 8, so it's feasible at any resolution (validated at 1280x800 AND 1024x1024 from the start). Animation: rows cascade-fade in top→bottom with the count-up; reduceMotion → static. Caught + fixed one bug pre-presentation: the rank badge was sized with a pixel value used as a relative split weight, so it ate half the row; now a proper proportional weight → small square badge. Verified valid across default/static/8-items/1-item/preSorted/empty.",
    "question": "First look at the Alpine leaderboard. Scrub it — rows cascade in, values count up, podium rows get a medal tint. Does the look land (badge size/shape, medal colors, podium tint strength, row spacing, name/value balance)? Open questions: (1) podium tint on by default — keep, or off? (2) the per-item Color column overrides the badge color — useful, or should badges always be medal/grey? I'll iterate one nudge at a time.",
